# DLINK - Link and capture a checked report

```text
B0:DLINK base
B0:DLINK output module [module ...]
```

## Build a program

From the writable drive containing PROGRAM.REL, run B0:DLINK PROGRAM.
DLINK invokes the supplied B0:LINK.COM and captures its report. Use
fresh output names for the .COM, .SYM and .LOG files.

## Several modules

```text
B0:DLINK RESULT MAIN PART
B0:DSYM RESULT.LOG
```

Use the same user area for output and modules. A complete successful
report is the input [DSYM](DSYM.HLP) needs to make disassembly symbols.
Check any failure before using the generated files.
